# Burn Engine servings & food-list gram weights

Complete agent reference for Burn & Build serving math.

**Source of truth:** `js/burnEngine.js` (`computeServingsPhase` loops). Macro-gram targets for scripts and audits: `js/burnEngineServingTargets.js`. Agents use **this doc** for semantics — do not re-derive serving criteria from scratch.

**This system does not use calories.** Users follow **servings** and weigh food to **gram portions** on the approved list. Never size portions, label PDFs, or explain the diet using calories.

> Engine implementation uses calorie-weighted loops in code only. That detail lives in `docs/burn-engine-internal-calorie-loops.md` — **do not use it for portions or UI.**

## Core principle

**A serving is defined by grams of the target macro, with a fat ceiling in grams.**

| Wrong | Right |
|-------|-------|
| Calorie targets per serving | **8g protein**, **14g carbs**, **10g carbs**, etc. |
| “Energy” or kcal for fruit portions | **18g carbs** per fruit serving |
| Weigh food without knowing prep state | Gram weight only valid for the **labeled prep** (dry / cooked / raw) |
| 1982 seminar gram weights on the 2026 list | **Current USDA (2026)** × Burn Engine slot formulas |

## 2026 food-list gram weights

The cutting diet food list uses **current USDA macros** (FoodData Central, 2026 reference in audit scripts) — not 1982 seminar test weights.

| Slot | Gram formula (2026 USDA) |
|------|--------------------------|
| P1 protein | `800 ÷ protein_per_100g` (step down if fat > 2g) |
| D1 milk | fit 8g pro + 12g carb + fat ceiling |
| D1 cultured dairy | P1-style (8g pro + fat ceiling) — cottage/yogurt/ricotta |
| G1 / S2 | `1400 ÷ carbs_per_100g` |
| VE | `1000 ÷ carbs_per_100g` |
| FQ | `1800 ÷ carbs_per_100g` |

Sync: `npm run sync:cutting-servings` · Audit: `npm run verify:cutting-servings`

Foods that exceed the fat ceiling at the full carb serving are flagged for review (may need roster trim).

